{"sections":[{"type":"Header","title":"Employment, unemployment and economic inactivity in South Somerset","label":"How South Somerset compares with the South West and Great Britain across employment-related statistics"},{"id":"mainlines","type":"Summary","title":"in South Somerset:","content":"<a name=\"section-top\"></a>","sections":[{"indicator":"Employment rate","value":"77.2%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Employment in South Somerset has increased compared with the previous year</p><p><a href=\"#section-employment\">Go to employment rate section</a></p>"},{"indicator":"Unemployment rate","value":"5.2%","age_band":"(ages 16+)","content":"<p>Unemployment (people looking for work) has fallen since a year earlier.</p><p><a href=\"#section-unemployment\">Go to unemployment rate section</a></p>"},{"indicator":"Claimant Count","value":"2.1%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Claimant Count was around the same in the year ending July 2023 than a year earlier. Claimant Count measures the number of people who are <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/aguidetolabourmarketstatistics#claimant-count\">claiming unemployment-related benefits.</a>  </p><p><a href=\"#section-claimant\">Go to Claimant Count section</a>  </p>"},{"indicator":"Economic inactivity","value":"2.1%","age_band":"(ages 16 to 64)","content":"<p>Economic inactivity has decreased since the previous year. These are people who are neither employed nor seeking work.</p><p><a href=\"#section-inactive\">Go to economic inactivity section</a></p>"}]},{"type":"Caveat","content":"<p>All estimates are based on the <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/surveys/informationforhouseholdsandindividuals/householdandindividualsurveys/labourforcesurvey\"> Labour Force Survey</a>. Data for local areas are based on smaller sample sizes than national figures and may vary more year to year.</p>"},{"type":"Employment_rate","content":"<a name=\"section-employment\"></a><h2>Employment in South Somerset has increased compared with the previous year</h2><p>South Somerset's employment rate was lower than across the South West as a whole in the year ending March 2023.</p><p>Of people aged 16 to 64 years living in South Somerset, 77.2% were employed in the year ending March 2023. This is an increase compared with the year ending March 2022 when the local rate was 72.0%.</p><p>Across the South West in the year ending  March 2023, 78.4% of people aged 16 to 64 years were employed. This was higher compared with the previous year, when 77.8% of people were employed.</p>"},{"id":"chart-timeseries","type":"Chart","chartType":"line-highlight","title":"Employment rate in the South West among those aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending 2012 to year ending March 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2012","y":72.1},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2013","y":73.2},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2014","y":73.9},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2015","y":74.5},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2016","y":76.1},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2017","y":76.1},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2018","y":76.6},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2019","y":81.2},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2020","y":77.9},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2021","y":80.5},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2022","y":78.3},{"z":"Bath and North East Somerset","x":"2023","y":75.4},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2012","y":69.9},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2013","y":71.1},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2014","y":69.9},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2015","y":72.9},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2016","y":74.9},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2017","y":76.2},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2018","y":78.1},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2019","y":77.6},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2020","